<title>AUSTRALIA: S.Australia says electricity unit important to budget.</title>
<headline>S.Australia says electricity unit important to budget.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Australian premier John Olsen on Thursday refused to rule out the sale of the state's electricity business in his next term of office, but said the industry's revenue flow outweighed any net worth in selling.</p>
<p>&quot;I cannot give you an indication one way or the other,&quot; Olsen told a news conference, when asked if he would rule out privatisation in his next term of office.</p>
<p>But he said the substantial and improving revenue and dividend flow from the Electricity Trust of SA (ETSA) was very important in balancing the state's budget.</p>
</text>
